{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1863 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "026dd18a51a561595abbc7d5ba279f6c936d29f03248dbb4cf324a426af319ab" :edb/db-before-t 1862 :edb/db-after-t 1863 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535175 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:44:20.191Z" 13194139535175 true] [17592186096619 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335552 13194139535175 true] [17592186096620 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335542 13194139535175 true] [17592186096620 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335545 13194139535175 true] [17592186097221 1100 "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-{e}^{3x}=0.\n$$" 13194139535175 true] [17592186097221 1100 "Solve the differential equation\n\n$\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} - e^{3x} = 0$." 13194139535175 false] [17592186097221 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}\\,{e}^{3x})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" 13194139535175 true] [17592186097221 1145 "The equation is $y''=e^{3x}$. Integrate twice:\n$$y'=\\frac13e^{3x}+C,\\qquad y=\\frac19e^{3x}+Cx+D.$$" 13194139535175 false] [17592186335542 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335543 13194139535175 true] [17592186335542 1089 "q-347842" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335542 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535175 true] [17592186335542 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $8x-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=5.$\n\n$y=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,+${{field-1}}" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335542 1113 #uuid "85b460c5-45ef-565d-85f6-70fe7fc6f047" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335542 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{x}^{2}+8x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-{x}^{2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(2)=5$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C \\\\ 5 & =-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}+4({2}^{2})+C \\\\ 5 & =-\\frac{8}{3}+16+C \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{40}{3}+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{25}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}-\\frac{25}{3}.\n$$" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335543 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335544 13194139535175 true] [17592186335543 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535175 true] [17592186335543 1041 "field-1" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335543 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335544 13194139535175 true] [17592186335543 1110 #uuid "2bc032f3-fbc1-54cb-8244-03c727fb366d" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335544 1034 "4x^2-\\frac{25}{3}" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335544 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535175 true] [17592186335544 1111 #uuid "ec6175a2-7628-54e2-9a83-5ea329ef75ec" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335545 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335546 13194139535175 true] [17592186335545 1089 "q-50044" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335545 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535175 true] [17592186335545 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=2$\n \n\n$$\nx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6{x}^{3}.\n$$" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335545 1113 #uuid "1eb154da-4739-51ad-b420-cb4dc79403e1" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335545 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=2{x}^{3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(-1)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{3}+C \\\\ 2 & =2(-1)^{3}+C \\\\ 2 & =-2+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{x}^{3}+4.\n$$" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335546 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335547 13194139535175 true] [17592186335546 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335548 13194139535175 true] [17592186335546 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335549 13194139535175 true] [17592186335546 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335550 13194139535175 true] [17592186335546 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335551 13194139535175 true] [17592186335546 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535175 true] [17592186335546 1041 "selection" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335546 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335551 13194139535175 true] [17592186335546 1110 #uuid "0367d76d-393f-563b-8a18-a5ef095afd09" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335547 1034 "y=6{x}^{3}+8" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335547 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535175 true] [17592186335547 1111 #uuid "39c37723-0d69-5949-9392-9e4a22784beb" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335548 1034 "y={x}^{3}+3" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335548 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535175 true] [17592186335548 1111 #uuid "f662054e-567a-5206-baa6-0c106c3270f0" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335549 1034 "y=-2{x}^{2}+4" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335549 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535175 true] [17592186335549 1111 #uuid "8506772a-2ec6-5eb3-a530-4e04ad831e12" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335550 1034 "y=3{x}^{2}-1" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335550 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535175 true] [17592186335550 1111 #uuid "a9fb4249-c501-5987-bf77-623752e67114" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335551 1034 "y=2{x}^{3}+4" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335551 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535175 true] [17592186335551 1111 #uuid "c99f4f6a-afd7-5903-ab46-48898f42996a" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335552 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335553 13194139535175 true] [17592186335552 1089 "q-79565" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335552 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535175 true] [17592186335552 1100 "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x?$" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335552 1113 #uuid "b7716424-9b11-538f-a06b-55bd73654360" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335552 1145 "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/fa13b048e5ca54c7074bbf6ec11421bfd8fb9e1618abd732a5faa1d78372a863.png)" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335554 13194139535175 true] [17592186335553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335555 13194139535175 true] [17592186335553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335556 13194139535175 true] [17592186335553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335557 13194139535175 true] [17592186335553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335558 13194139535175 true] [17592186335553 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535175 true] [17592186335553 1041 "selection" 13194139535175 true] [17592186335553 1104 #edb/ref 17